From 50d00daff5f8a612da1688403080c981d932ebcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:31:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: omci: treat an erased identity NVMEM cell as absent

Vendor flash keeps the GPON serial in a record that is left erased
until an ISP serial is provisioned. Reading such a cell returned an
all-0xff buffer, the serial parser rejected it and the whole xPON probe
failed, so boards could not describe the cell unconditionally.

Skip all-0xff cells so the MAC-derived or random fallback still applies.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/identity.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/identity.c b/net/xpon/omci/identity.c
index d71cc8caf..1bc9dcf05 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/identity.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/identity.c
@@ -367,7 +367,11 @@ static int omci_identity_read_cell(struct device *dev,
 	nvmem_cell_put(cell);
 	if (IS_ERR(data))
 		return PTR_ERR(data);
-	ret = setter(identity, data, len, OMCI_CONFIG_SOURCE_NVMEM);
+	/* An unprovisioned flash cell reads back erased: treat it as absent. */
+	if (!memchr_inv(data, 0xff, len))
+		ret = 0;
+	else
+		ret = setter(identity, data, len, OMCI_CONFIG_SOURCE_NVMEM);
 	kfree(data);
 	return ret;
 }
